# Engine files that include a PLATFORM header.
#
# EMPTY, and that is the point. engine/ names no platform header at all: the
# compiler spellings it needs are engine/compiler.h, a typed load out of bytes is
# engine/nnue/nnue_common.h, the huge page size arrives as a field on the arena
# seam, and a worker's history bank is an index into the engine's own map rather
# than a handle on the host's topology.
#
# tests/linkcheck.sh cannot replace this file. It reasons about symbols an object
# leaves undefined, and a dependency carried by a header leaves none -- an inline
# function, a class used only as a member, a constexpr that folds. Both linkcheck
# baselines were empty while nineteen of these edges existed.
#
# Keep it empty. The next platform header included from engine/ fails the gate
# rather than joining a list.
